		\cf5 // Wall characteristics are convolved with reflection order impulse responses to make a \cf2 \
		\cf5 // rich array of options in which the range of reflection orders and array of wall \cf2 \
		\cf5 // sequence patterns become distinguished by differences of color and sound shape. \cf2 \
		\cf5 // The following parameters for specifying and controlling wall impulse responses, \cf2 \
		\cf5 // save some adjustments, function similarly to reflection order impulse response\cf2 \
		\cf5 // parameters. \cf2 \
		\cf5 //\cf2 \
		\cf5 // Walls, by default, are given a single pulse impulse response. The default pulse may be \cf2 \
		\cf5 // used as-is or be replaced by impulse responses read in from selected channels of a sound\cf2 \
		\cf5 //  file, according to the parameters and file specifications supplied through the parameters below. \cf2 \
		\cf5 // Using the code specified in the wall convolution mode and the wall sequences it \cf2 \
		\cf5 // identifies, impulse response sequences may be convolved together to add distinguishing\cf2 \
		\cf5 // colors to the reflection. \cf2 \
		\cf5 //\cf2 \
		\cf5 // Band pass filtering may be applied to the wall impulse responses, be they file-determined \cf2 \
		\cf5 // or default pulses. Filtering may be applied either once, as an input pre-processing of the \cf2 \
		\cf5 // pulse or file-determined responses, or multiple times, following the successive convolutions,  \cf2 \
		\cf5 // which in default pulse mode take the place of the wall impulse response convolution. \cf2 \
		\cf5 //\cf2 \
		\cf5 // Sound file wall impulse responses may be balanced against the default pulse, which takes \cf2 \
		\cf5 // place in a pre-processing stage, the same as with reflection order impulse responses. \cf2 \
\
\
